Source-Makefile: package/feeds/packages/fping/Makefile

Package: fping
Version: 5.0-1
Depends: +libc 
Conflicts: 
Menu-Depends: 
Provides: 
Section: net
Category: Network
Repository: packages
Title: sends ICMP ECHO_REQUEST packets to network hosts
Maintainer: Nikil Mehta <nikil.mehta@gmail.com>
Source: fping-5.0.tar.gz
License: BSD-4-Clause
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Type: ipkg
Description:   fping is a ping like program which uses the Internet Control Message Protocol
  (ICMP) echo request to determine if a target host is responding.  fping
  differs from ping in that you can specify any number of targets on the command
  line, or specify a file containing the lists of targets to ping.  Instead of
  sending to one target until it times out or replies, fping will send out a
  ping packet and move on to the next target in a round-robin fashion.
https://fping.org/
Nikil Mehta <nikil.mehta@gmail.com>
@@


